    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests are green. The full suite consists of `AcceptanceTest` (the only concrete test class; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract), which now passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` de-duplication in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**The change:** Previously the customer code was a pure function of the owner's identity fields (`<REGION>-<HASH8>`), so two owners whose normalized telephone + last name hashed identically would get the same code. Per the spec, on a collision the code now gets `-<n>` appended with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Wrapped the code assignment in `createOwner` with a new `deduplicateCustomerCode(...)` call.\n2. Added the `deduplicateCustomerCode` helper, which gathers the customer codes already held by existing owners; if the base code is free it's returned as-is, otherwise it tries `base-2`, `base-3`, \u2026 until it finds one no existing owner holds.\n3. Added the `java.util.stream.Collectors` import.\n\nThe `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` acceptance test (asserting distinct owners always get distinct customer codes) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
